      "description": "Career Services :: Mayville State University :: Mayville, ND Facebook X / Twitter YouTube Instagram Search Why MSU Visit Us Directory Alumni & Friends Community About MSU BlackBoard Email Sharepoint Campus Connection Starfish Future Students Freshmen Transfer Students Re-Admit Students Future Comet Athlete International & Canadian Students Graduate Students Adult Learners/Non-Degree Seekers Dual Credit Students Veterans & Military See the 2026-27 Viewbook Scholarships Campus Tours & Virtual Visits Admissions Make It Mayville State! Request Information Contact us ... we're here to help! Admitted to MSU ... Next Steps! Apply for On Campus Housing Academics Academics Majors & Minors Accreditation Teacher Education Graduate Studies MSU Online Study Abroad Office of Academic Records Catalog & Calendar Schedules, Dates & Deadlines Class Attendance and Participation Starfish Center for Teaching and Learning Summer School 2026 Paying for School Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Scholarships Business Office Net Price Calculator Exceptional Value Federal Tax Benefits Inceptia/Return to Student Loan Repayment Life on Campus Campus Living Residence Halls Apply for On Campus Housing Questions about Housing Dining Services Things To Do On-Campus Employment Report a Concern MSU Online MSU Online Online and Distance Programs Getting Started with Online Classes Online Course Schedule A&P Registration Contact Us Distance & Online Admissions Distance Student Services FAQs Instructional Technology State Authorization & Professional Licensure Information Student Complaint Process Student Resources Student Resources Academic Advising Bookstore Campus Connection Career Services Counseling Disability Support Services Hazing Health Services Information Technology Services Library Mailroom Preparing to Graduate Sexual Violence & Substance Abuse Prevention Resources SharePoint Student Success Center Testing Veterans & Military Writing Center Report a Concern Career Services Home Student Resources Career Services CAREER SERVICES Career Services serves as a resource for: Students and alumni seeking assistance with career development Primary point of contact for employers to connect with Mayville State students and alumni CAREER PLANNING ASSISTANCE Career Services provides career planning tools to help students find their career path, including one-on-one career advisement and access to career planning resources . CAREER SEARCH ASSISTANCE Students and alumni are offered assistance to help find appropriate and satisfying employment.  Services include: Job search strategies Resume and cover letter writing Mock interviews Information on area career fairs and on-campus employer engagement events Contact Career Services to make an appointment or email your resume and cover letter for review. Ready to get started with Handshake or look for on-campus student employment? INTERNSHIPS Mayville State University students, of any major, have the opportunity to work in a field related to their major and earn credit for their work experience. Mayville State students have completed internships across the United States in private companies, governmental agencies, and non-profit organizations. Students can begin the internship registration process by contacting Career Services . SHARING OPPORTUNITIES WITH MAYVILLE STATE Thank you for your interest in sharing your career and internship opportunities with us.  You may post your opportunities with Mayville State through Handshake, our online career management platform. SUCCESS OF OUR GRADUATES Career outcomes report is prepared by Career Services and details the career outcomes of past Mayville State graduates. 2020 Career Outcome Report 2019 Career Outcome Report 2016-18 Career Outcome Compilation 2015-17 Career Outcome Compilation 2014-16 Career Outcome Compilation CAREER SERVICES PROFESSIONAL AFFILIATIONS North Dakota Association of Career Services Professionals (NDACSP) National Association of Colleges and Employers (NACE) American Association for Employment in Education MISSION STATEMENT To promote greater awareness within Mayville State University of issues related to the field of career planning and the world of employment, as they affect persons over their lifetimes. To assist students and alumni as they engage in self-assessment, obtain occupational information, explore employment opportunities or advanced education, and to present themselves effectively as candidates. Our ultimate goal is to provide resources that allow and enhance optimal placement in employment or further professional preparation for the greatest number of Mayville State University students and alumni. Shanna Hanson Career Services & Belonging Coordinator BQ Library, Lower Level 701-788-4649 Career Planning Handshake Events Graduate Survey Mayville State Job Fair What’s important for my students is having the chance to advance their careers through research opportunities. They might not get or have access to those at other institutions. They can present their work at local, regional, and international levels. Imagine that scope! - Dr. Joseph Mehus Academics Admissions Paying for School Campus Living Request Information Visit Us Apply Online Directory Site Search About MSU More Info Accreditation News Events Athletics Consumer Information Title IX Notice of Nondiscrimination Policies & Procedures Alumni & Friends Events Stay Connected Capital Projects MSU Foundation Transcript Requests Give to MSU Community Child Care Wellness Center Pool Education & Innovation Center Arts MSU Online Employment Emergencies Contact Us Report a Concern Report Accessibility Issue Facebook X / Twitter YouTube Instagram Site Map Privacy Policy © 2026 Mayville State University"
